## Dependencies

`nuxt`, `vue` and `vue-router` are **devDependencies**: `nuxt build` writes a self-contained `.output/` (server plus
the runtime packages it traced), and the production image runs only `.output`. `npm audit --omit=dev` therefore
audits what ships. Known advisories without a fix at the time of generation live only in Nuxt's build/dev toolchain
and never reach `.output`: `braces` (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm, via nitropack's globby) and `node-forge`
(GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv, via listhen's dev HTTPS certificates). Re-check with `npm audit` when upgrading Nuxt.

{{end -}}
## Testing

- `npm test`: BFF unit tests (sealing, CSRF, path allowlist, login, proxy, refresh) with a mocked API.
- `make test-e2e`: Playwright against a **production build** and `e2e/mock-api.mjs` — login, protected page, logout,
  no token in `document.cookie`/storage, no CSP violations; the theme toggle (OS default, override, persistence).
- `make ui-shots`: the same build, a screenshot of every screen at 375, 768 and 1280 px in light and dark into `ui-shots/`
  (git-ignored: open them and look); fails on horizontal overflow, console errors or a screen without the toggle.
